BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ca779c654244651a@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260728T192425Z
DTSTART:20260801T123000Z
DTEND:20260801T143000Z
SUMMARY:Nar-Hari: 6 Verses from Shri Guru Granth Sahib & Panchvani
LOCATION:C.D. Deshmukh Auditorium\, IIC main\, India International Centre
 \, 40 Max Mueller Marg\, Lodhi Gardens\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://iicdelhi.in/programmes/nar-hari-6-verses-shri-guru-granth-sah
 ib-panchvani
DESCRIPTION:Nar-Hari: 6 Verses from Shri Guru Granth Sahib & Panchvani\nA
 n Inclusive Sankirtan where Music\, Mysticism & Spirituality Meet Science
 \nPerformers: Ayush Jha\, vocalist and/or on Harmonium\; Kanha Trehan\, v
 ocalist & with khartaal\; Rajat Kanungo\, vocalist and/or on harmonium\; 
 Sanvi Katoch\, vocalist and/or on harmonium\; Dr Sangeeta\, vocalist and/
 or on harmonium\; Satvik on Tabla\; Amar on Guitar\; Pragshu on Cajun\; A
 nya Katoch\, chorus singer\nGuest of Honour & Patron: Prof. Charanjit Sin
 gh Shah\, Chairman & Founder\, Creative Group LLP\nPerformance inspired b
 y the teachings of the 15th-century Bhakti saint Ravidas\, whose composit
 ions are enshrined in both the Shri Guru Granth Sahib and Panchvani. Blen
 ding devotional music\, participatory Sankirtan and narration\, the progr
 amme explores the dialogue between spirituality and contemporary scientif
 ic thought\, offering a reflective experience that celebrates joy\, inclu
 sivity and inner transformation.\n\nhttps://iicdelhi.in/programmes/nar-ha
 ri-6-verses-shri-guru-granth-sahib-panchvani
CATEGORIES:performance\,music
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:24e9036b4f99823f@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260728T192425Z
DTSTART:20260801T133000Z
DTEND:20260801T153000Z
SUMMARY:Bhupen Da Uncut
LOCATION:Gulmohar\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1328
DESCRIPTION:Birth Centenary of Dr. Bhupen Hazarika . Bhupen Da Uncut (Doc
 u/2025/Assamese with English subtitles/65 mins) Dir. Bobbeeta Sharma . A 
 rare\, vintage first-person account filmed 25 years ago in London\, where
  the legendary maestro reflects on his extraordinary journey. The documen
 tary follows Dr. Hazarika as he speaks intimately about his childhood\, t
 he profound influence of Assamese cinema pioneer Jyoti Prasad Agarwala\, 
 his higher studies in New York\, and the dynamics of his relationship wit
 h his wife\, Priyamvada Patel. Offering a window into his mind and philos
 ophy\, Bhupen Da Uncut features the legend reciting several of his unpubl
 ished poems\, capturing the essence of the man and his masterpieces. Scre
 ening followed by a discussion with Bobbeeta Sharma \, director\; Chinmoy
  Sharma \, executive producer\; Ravindra Badgaiyan \, editor .\n\nhttps:/
 /indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1328
CATEGORIES:film\,cinema
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3d17aaac2ea9ba66@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260728T192425Z
DTSTART:20260801T140000Z
DTEND:20260801T160000Z
SUMMARY:The Big Fat City
LOCATION:The Stein Auditorium\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New D
 elhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1329
DESCRIPTION:The Big Fat City (Hindi/90 mins) Wri. Mahesh Dattani . Dir. S
 hilpi Marwaha . A thought-provoking drama that explores the complexities 
 of urban life in Mumbai. The story revolves around Murli and his wife\, w
 ho are struggling to pay off their loan after Murli loses his job. Desper
 ate for financial help\, they host a dinner for Murli’s former collegem
 ate\, hoping he can secure them another loan. The arrival of their neighb
 our\, a TV actress with her own financial troubles and a drunken husband\
 , complicates the situation. The play explores how financial stress strai
 ns relationships while revealing the harsh realities behind the glamouriz
 ed version of city life. Prod. Sukhmanch Theatre . Tickets at Rs.500\, Rs
 .350 & Rs.200 are available online on bookmyshow.com and at the Habitat P
 rogrammes desk .\n\nhttps://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1329
CATEGORIES:performance\,theatre
END:VEVENT
