SUMMARY:Sawani - Jugalbandi
LOCATION:The Theatre\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New Delhi 1100
 03
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1331
DESCRIPTION:Sawani - Jugalbandi by Aastha Goswami (Vocals) and Dr. Chandr
 ima Majumdar (Sarod)\, featuring monsoon ragas\, soulful Kajri\, Jhoola\,
  and sawan ke geet from Banarasi and Braj traditions celebrating the rain
 y season as a timeless source of inspiration. Accompanied by Akhtar Hassa
 n on Tabla and Lalit Sisodia on Harmonium. Collab. Culturally Active Delh
 iites .\n\nhttps://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1331
CATEGORIES:performance\,music
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:08a76e09e95f1990@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260728T192425Z
DTSTART:20260802T133000Z
DTEND:20260802T153000Z
SUMMARY:She Walked Anyway
LOCATION:Casuarina\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1332
DESCRIPTION:Book Launch & Discussion . She Walked Anyway by Dr. Sazina Kh
 an . A collection of poems and a lyrical meditation on quiet courage\, in
 ner reclamation\, and the profound strength of moving forward without per
 mission or validation. Through evocative poems such as Unannounced Becomi
 ng\, Permissionless\, Grace\, Unrequested\, The Yes I Gave Myself\, and B
 ecoming Without Allowance \, this collection traces the inner evolution o
 f a woman who chooses motion over hesitation and self-trust over approval
 . Publisher: White Falcon . The author will be in conversation on Walking
  Through Storms: Women\, Memory and the Making of the Inner Self with Oro
 on Das \, actor\, theatre artist and Dr. Gilles Chuyen \, director\, chor
 eographer\, actor. Moderator: Meera Khanna \, writer\, poet\, Trustee & P
 resident\, The Guild for Service. Chief Guest: Prof. (Dr.) K. G. Suresh \
 , Director\, India Habitat Centre.\n\nhttps://indiahabitat.org/Events_det
 ails/1332
CATEGORIES:talk\,literature
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:83809c05335c0e0e@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260728T192425Z
DTSTART:20260802T140000Z
DTEND:20260802T160000Z
SUMMARY:The House of Bernarda Alba
LOCATION:The Stein Auditorium\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New D
 elhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1333
DESCRIPTION:The House of Bernarda Alba (English/130 mins with interval) D
 esign & Direction by Shomik Ray . Written by Spanish playwright\, Federic
 o García Lorca in June 1936\, during the turbulent period of the Spanish
  Revolution. The play explores domestic oppression\, love\, desire\, and 
 betrayal while serving as a powerful reflection on authoritarian systems 
 that suppress individual voices in the name of society. Through Bernarda 
 Alba’s household\, Lorca examines themes of power\, control\, repressio
 n\, and the human longing for freedom\, combining emotional conflict\, da
 rk humour\, and violence into a timeless theatrical experience. Prod. Sha
 pno Ekhon . Tickets at Rs.500\, Rs.350 & Rs.200 are available online on b
 ookmyshow.com and at the Habitat Programmes desk .\n\nhttps://indiahabita
 t.org/Events_details/1333
CATEGORIES:performance\,theatre
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:59b4524881b34779@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260728T192425Z
DTSTART:20260803T130000Z
DTEND:20260803T150000Z
SUMMARY:Archival Echoes of a Folk Lute in the Indian Himalaya
LOCATION:Conference Room I\, IIC main\, India International Centre\, 40 M
 ax Mueller Marg\, Lodhi Gardens\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://iicdelhi.in/programmes/archival-echoes-folk-lute-indian-himal
 aya
DESCRIPTION:Archival Echoes of a Folk Lute in the Indian Himalaya\nSpeake
 r: Dr. Katherine Freeze Wolf\, Independent scholar\, with PhD in Musicolo
 gy and Ethnomusicology\, Brown University.\nModerator: Shubha Chaudhuri\,
  Associate Director General (Academic)\, Archives and Research Centre for
  Ethnomusicology\, American Institute of Indian Studies\nThe speaker will
  share their experience studying the Western Tibetan folk lute gowo (call
 ed ko-phongs in Ladakhi) in Ladakh\, and the repatriation of musical reco
 rdings made between the 1930s and 1970s. The talk will explore the signif
 icance of these recordings in understanding the instrument's diverse perf
 ormance styles\, song ecologies and heritage narratives.\n\nhttps://iicde
 lhi.in/programmes/archival-echoes-folk-lute-indian-himalaya
CATEGORIES:talk
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d63b893a4a2d8691@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260728T192425Z
DTSTART:20260803T130000Z
DTEND:20260803T150000Z
SUMMARY:Cleaning Transport – Tackling Vehicular Emissions and the Futur
 e of Mobility Uniting Science\, Health\, Policy & People
LOCATION:Lecture Room II\, IIC Annexe\, India International Centre\, 40 M
 ax Mueller Marg\, Lodhi Gardens\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://iicdelhi.in/programmes/cleaning-transport-tackling-vehicular-
 emissions-and-future-mobility-uniting-science
DESCRIPTION:Cleaning Transport – Tackling Vehicular Emissions and the F
 uture of Mobility\nUniting Science\, Health\, Policy & People\nModerator:
  Sarika Panda\, Co-founder\, Raahgiri Foundation and Director\, Nagarro\n
 Discussants: Dr. Virinder Sharma\, Member (Technical)\, CAQM\; Niharika R
 ai\, Secretary-cum-Commissioner\, Transport Dpt\, Govt of NCT of Delhi\; 
 Mahmood Ahmed\, Additional Secretary (Transport)\, Ministry of Road Trans
 port and Highways\; J. Ganesan\, Chairman\, Haryana State Pollution Contr
 ol Board\; Amit Bhatt\, India Managing Director\, International Council o
 n Clean Transportation\; Trupti Deshpande\, Energiva Ventures\nTransition
 ing to clean urban mobility yields profound benefits—ranging from impro
 ved air quality and reduced greenhouse gas emissions to quieter and more 
 livable cities. This session will explore how to accelerate the shift tow
 ard zero-emission transport by scaling up electric vehicle ecosystems\, m
 odernizing public transit networks\, and enforcing stringent emission reg
 ulations.\nThis is the fourth discussion in the series of dialogues under
  the umbrella of ‘Uniting Science\, Health\, Policy & People’\n(Colla
 boration: Commission for Air Quality Management (CAQM) and Raahgiri Found
 ation)\n\nhttps://iicdelhi.in/programmes/cleaning-transport-tackling-vehi
 cular-emissions-and-future-mobility-uniting-science
CATEGORIES:talk\,science\,sociology
END:VEVENT
