SUMMARY:Bharat Bodh: A National Seminar on India’s Knowledge Traditions
LOCATION:Gulmohar\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1356
DESCRIPTION:Bharat Bodh: A National Seminar on India’s Knowledge Tradit
 ions . Presented by the Bharat Bodh Kendra \, Habitat Library & Research 
 Centre & Anjana Welfare Society . A discussion on the relevance of India
 ’s knowledge traditions in contemporary education\, inspired by the Nat
 ional Education Policy (NEP) 2020 and Indian Knowledge Systems (IKS). Spe
 akers: Guru Nalini & Kamalini Asthana \, Kathak exponents\; Maya Kulshres
 htha \, Kathak artist\; Dr. Karunashankar Upadhyay \, Professor & Head\, 
 Department of Hindi\, University of Mumbai\; Prof. (Dr.) K. G. Suresh \, 
 Director\, India Habitat Centre..\n\nhttps://indiahabitat.org/Events_deta
 ils/1356
